From 3fcf3e7c8c40e57e9a56f50b5d4ef4384ed37e66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:48:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] mifare: an unreadable MAD is a tag without NDEF, not an
 absent tag

A MIFARE Classic that was never NDEF formatted, or whose sector keys are
not the public ones, fails the MAD authentication every time it is read.
mifare_release() turns that error into near_adapter_disconnect(), so the
tag leaves D-Bus, and with ConstantPoll it is immediately found again,
dropped again, and so on for as long as the card lies on the antenna.

Measured on a Pixel 2 XL running mainline Linux: a Classic 1K badge
cycled add and remove roughly every 3 seconds while lying still, the tag
re-appearing 49 to 53ms after each removal. To an application this is
indistinguishable from someone repeatedly tapping the card.

Report a tag carrying no NDEF and leave it connected. Whether it is
still in the field is the presence check's question, and that check is
equipped to answer it.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 plugins/mifare.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plugins/mifare.c b/plugins/mifare.c
index f42007d..d749cc2 100644
--- a/plugins/mifare.c
+++ b/plugins/mifare.c
@@ -734,8 +734,26 @@ static int mifare_read_MAD1(uint8_t *resp, int length, void *data)
 	DBG("%p %d", data, length);
 
 	if (length < 0) {
-		err = length;
-		return err;
+		/*
+		 * The MAD authentication failed. That is not a tag leaving the
+		 * field: a MIFARE Classic that was never NDEF formatted, or
+		 * whose sector keys are not the public ones, answers exactly
+		 * like this every time it is read. Reporting an error here
+		 * makes mifare_release() disconnect the adapter, so the tag
+		 * disappears from D-Bus and, with ConstantPoll, is found and
+		 * dropped again every few seconds for as long as it sits on
+		 * the antenna.
+		 *
+		 * Report a tag with no NDEF instead and leave it connected.
+		 * Whether it is still there is the presence check's question,
+		 * and it is the one equipped to answer it.
+		 */
+		DBG("No readable MAD: tag carries no NDEF");
+
+		if (mf_ck->cb)
+			mf_ck->cb(mf_ck->adapter_idx, mf_ck->target_idx, 0);
+
+		return mifare_release(0, mf_ck);
 	}
 
 	/*
